{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1664","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1664","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1664\",\"parent_revision\":\"b2cb7e7e8412e5fce773d644bb35d210b43e0011\",\"root_revision\":\"f0462cc1169aae0d4c60cc9ee414d56764690558ba2aeec2af2d11cd9878f206\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_view` called with `summary=False` (needed to read actual content) returns the full `ViewItemResult` dict unconditionally. For groomed items with large bodies (e.g. #996 at 57KB), this produces ~14.8k token MCP responses.\\n\\n**Confirmed defect location:** `server.py:1677\u20131681` \u2014 the `summary=False` branch has no token budget guard before returning `full_response`.\\n\\nThe `summary=True` default path already returns a compact manifest correctly. The gap is that agents following the `_hint` (calling `summary=False` to fetch actual content) are exposed to large responses with no size guard.\\n\\n**The `backlog_list` tool already implements `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` with tiktoken auto-pagination.** `backlog_view` should adopt the same pattern.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect \u2014 missing auto-compaction guard in `summary=False` code path\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`, `_auto_compact_view_response`, token guard in `backlog_view` lines 1677\u20131681\\n\\n**Tests (new):**\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 add `TestBacklogViewAutoCompaction` class\\n\\n**No changes needed:**\\n- `operations.py`, `models.py`, skills/agents (already use progressive disclosure pattern)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Direct callers exposed:**\\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- `skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md`\\n- `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`\\n- `skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`\\n- `agents/impact-analyst.md`\\n- `agents/plan-validator.md`\\n- `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**Backward compatibility:** `summary=True` default path is unaffected. Only `summary=False` callers on large items are affected.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P1** \u2014 context window exhaustion is directly user-facing. One call on a groomed item consumes ~37% of a 40k-token context window. Agents in multi-step workflows (groom, work, validate) calling `backlog_view` several times will exhaust context before completing the task.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=<large-item>, summary=False)` \u2014 when full response exceeds 4,400 tokens (cl100k_base) \u2014 returns auto-compact form instead of full body\\n- [ ] Auto-compact form contains: (1) identity fields, (2) item `description`, (3) `sections_index` string (existing `[N] Title (M entries)` format), (4) full token count, (5) instructions for targeted follow-up via `section=` parameter\\n- [ ] Auto-compact response is under 4,400 tokens\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(summary=False, section=\\\"<specific-section>\\\")` \u2014 when section-filtered response exceeds 4,400 tokens \u2014 returns auto-compact limited to matched sections with truncation notice\\n- [ ] `backlog_view` on a small item (within budget) returns full response unchanged \u2014 no regression\\n- [ ] New constant `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` defined adjacent to `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` using same `_enc` encoder\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(summary=True)` behavior unchanged \u2014 existing tests pass unmodified\\n- [ ] New tests: (a) large body triggers auto-compact, (b) small body returns full, (c) auto-compact includes `sections_index` and `_hint`, (d) auto-compact token count within budget\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**S (small)** \u2014 ~3 hours total\\n\\n- Core change: ~20 lines in `server.py`\\n- Tests: copy and adapt from existing `backlog_list` token-budget tests\\n- No schema, model, or migration changes\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Identify a groomed item with large body (e.g. #996, 57KB)\\n2. Call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#996\\\", summary=False)` \u2192 full body returned, ~14.8k tokens\\n3. Call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#996\\\", summary=False, section=\\\"Acceptance Criteria\\\")` \u2192 still ~14.8k tokens (full metadata always included regardless of section filter)\\n4. Call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#996\\\", summary=True)` \u2192 compact manifest, small response \u2014 **this path works correctly**\\n\\nThe defect bites agents that must use `summary=False` to read actual content.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using backlog MCP tools in agent workflows**, I want **`backlog_view` to auto-compact large responses instead of returning the full body unconditionally** so that **a single tool call does not consume ~37% of the agent context window**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User observation \u2014 backlog_view of #996 in session 2026-04-08\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-08\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-24)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [x] `backlog_view(selector=<large-item>, summary=False)` \u2014 when full response exceeds token budget \u2014 returns auto-compact form instead of full body (`_over_budget=True` in response)\\n- [x] Auto-compact form contains: identity fields (`number`, `title`, `priority`, `status`), `description`, `sections_index`, `_full_chars`, `_usage` (caller instructions for targeted follow-up)\\n- [x] `backlog_view` on a small item (within budget) returns full response unchanged \u2014 no regression\\n- [x] `sections=` filter bypasses auto-compact \u2014 caller has already narrowed scope\\n- [x] `section=` filter bypasses auto-compact \u2014 caller has already narrowed scope\\n- [x] `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` defined adjacent to `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` using same `_enc` encoder\\n- [x] `backlog_view(summary=True)` behavior unchanged\\n- [x] Tests: (a) large body triggers auto-compact, (b) small body returns full, (c) auto-compact bypassed with `sections=`, (d) auto-compact bypassed with `section=`\\n- [ ] **OPEN \u2014 follow-up only**: Force `include_content=False` on `view_item` call when `summary=True` to avoid assembling 57KB body only to discard it. Tracked as separate issue.\\n\\n**Note:** `_auto_compact_view_response` from the original Implementation Notes was not used \u2014 the final implementation uses `_build_over_budget_view` with a slightly different field set (`_usage` instead of `_hint`, includes `number` and `status`). Behavior is equivalent or better.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Changed (verified in source):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`, `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD`, `_build_over_budget_view()`, token guard in `backlog_view` lines 1849\u20131871\\n\\n**Tests added (verified in source):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 4 new tests: `test_build_over_budget_view_includes_all_nine_fields`, `test_build_over_budget_view_usage_mentions_sections_param`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_triggers_when_over_token_budget`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_not_triggered_when_under_token_budget`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_bypassed_when_sections_filter_provided`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_bypassed_when_section_filter_provided`\\n\\n**No changes needed:**\\n- `operations.py`, `models.py`, skills/agents (already use progressive disclosure pattern)\\n\\n**Follow-up (separate issue):**\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 force `include_content=False` when `summary=True` to avoid assembling full body only to discard it\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Direct callers of `backlog_view(summary=False)`:**\\n\\n| File | Usage |\\n|---|---|\\n| `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` | `summary=False` call |\\n| `agents/impact-analyst.md` | `summary=False` call |\\n| `agents/classifier.md` | `summary=False` call |\\n| `agents/alignment-analyst.md` | `summary=False` call |\\n\\nSkills listed in the Impact section (`groom-backlog-item`, `dispatch`, `add-new-feature`, `complete-implementation`, `work-milestone`) and agents (`plan-validator`) were not found to use `summary=False` directly \u2014 they likely use `summary=True` (the default) and follow progressive disclosure.\\n\\n**Backward compatibility:** `summary=True` default path is unaffected. Callers using `section=` or `sections=` filters bypass auto-compact and receive their filtered result unchanged.\\n\\n### Implementation Status\\n\\n**The primary defect fix is already implemented.** Verification of actual server.py state:\\n\\n- `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` \u2014 defined at line 67 (adjacent to `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` at line 62)\\n- `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD = _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET * 4` \u2014 heuristic pre-check at line 76\\n- `_build_over_budget_view()` \u2014 defined at lines 1701\u20131740; returns compact dict with `number`, `title`, `priority`, `status`, `description`, `_over_budget=True`, `_full_chars`, `_usage`, and `sections_index`\\n- Guard in `backlog_view` `summary=False` branch \u2014 lines 1859\u20131870: body-length heuristic pre-check followed by precise token count check; returns `_build_over_budget_view()` when over budget\\n- `sections=` filter bypasses auto-compact (caller has already narrowed) \u2014 line 1851\u20131852\\n- `section=` filter bypasses auto-compact \u2014 line 1859 condition\\n\\nThe item description referenced `server.py:1677\u20131681` as the defect location; the actual implementation now sits at lines 1848\u20131872 due to code growth. The fix is behaviorally complete.\\n\\n**One divergence from the original AC:** `_build_over_budget_view` uses `_usage` key (not `_hint`) and returns 8 fields including `number` and `status` \u2014 the original AC specified `_hint` and omitted `number`/`status`. The implemented form is more informative.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Fix `backlog_view summary=False` unbounded response |\\n| Defect location | PRESENT \u2014 **already fixed** | `server.py:1849\u20131871` implements `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`, body heuristic, and `_build_over_budget_view` |\\n| Token-budget pattern | PRESENT | `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000`, `_VIEW_BODY_CHARS_THRESHOLD = _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET * 4`, `_token_count()` |\\n| Tests | PRESENT \u2014 4 tests exist | `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_triggers_when_over_token_budget`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_not_triggered_when_under_token_budget`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_bypassed_when_sections_filter_provided`, `test_backlog_view_auto_compact_bypassed_when_section_filter_provided` |\\n| Follow-up optimization | MISSING \u2014 not tracked | Force `include_content=False` on `view_item` call when `summary=True` to avoid assembling 57KB body only to discard it |\\n\\n**Gap**: The follow-up optimization (avoid assembling full body when `summary=True`) is not implemented and has no separate tracking issue.\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis 5 Whys\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `backlog_view(summary=False)` returns full `ViewItemResult.model_dump()` with no size check\\n2. No `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` constant exists \u2014 token-budget pattern was only implemented for `backlog_list`\\n3. When `summary=True` was added, it solved \\\"accidental full-load on first call\\\" but no fallback was added for large `summary=False` responses\\n4. The `section=` filter operates on sections dict keys only \u2014 does not reduce the full serialised response enough for very large items\\n5. Content selection and response size were not unified \u2014 `_filter_view_sections` has no token-counting logic\\n\\n**Root cause statement:** When `backlog_view` is called with `summary=False`, no token budget guard exists; the full serialised item body is returned unconditionally.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**New constant and helper (add after line 61 in `server.py`):**\\n\\n```python\\n_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400  # adjacent to _LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET\\n\\ndef _auto_compact_view_response(\\n    full_response: dict[str, object],\\n    result: ViewItemResult,\\n    selector: str,\\n) -> dict[str, object]:\\n    full_tokens = len(_enc.encode(json.dumps(full_response)))\\n    compact: dict[str, object] = {\\n        \\\"title\\\": result.title,\\n        \\\"priority\\\": result.priority,\\n        \\\"issue\\\": result.issue,\\n        \\\"description\\\": result.description,\\n        \\\"_auto_compacted\\\": True,\\n        \\\"_full_tokens\\\": full_tokens,\\n        \\\"_hint\\\": (\\n            f\\\"Response exceeded token budget. Load specific sections:\\\\n\\\"\\n            f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='<name>')\\\\n\\\"\\n            f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, include_content=False)\\\"\\n        ),\\n    }\\n    if result.sections_index:\\n        compact[\\\"sections_index\\\"] = result.sections_index\\n    return compact\\n```\\n\\n**Guard in `backlog_view` (replace lines 1677\u20131681):**\\n\\n```python\\nif not summary:\\n    if sections is not None:\\n        full_response = _filter_view_sections(full_response, sections)\\n    token_count = len(_enc.encode(json.dumps(full_response)))\\n    if token_count > _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET:\\n        return _auto_compact_view_response(full_response, result, selector)\\n    return full_response\\n```\\n\\n**Follow-up (separate issue):** When `summary=True`, force `include_content=False` on the `operations.view_item` call to avoid assembling 57KB body only to discard it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis (5-Whys)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `backlog_view(summary=False)` returns full `ViewItemResult.model_dump()` with no size check\\n2. No `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` constant exists \u2014 token-budget pattern was only implemented for `backlog_list`\\n3. When `summary=True` was added, it solved \\\"accidental full-load on first call\\\" but no fallback was added for large `summary=False` responses\\n4. The `section=` filter operates on sections dict keys only \u2014 does not reduce the full serialised response enough for very large items\\n5. Content selection and response size were not unified \u2014 `_filter_view_sections` has no token-counting logic\\n\\n**Root cause statement:** When `backlog_view` is called with `summary=False`, no token budget guard exists; the full serialised item body is returned unconditionally.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"52833906783faf6adb2b42d2459ed2e4d24cdb297516458996a6fa3560149aa6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg7DKA\"}"}